# What this repository is for: the work that cannot be regenerated.
#
# The test for keeping a file is whether losing it would cost anything other
# than compute. Everything excluded below rebuilds deterministically from the
# uclcovid archive, which has its own git history and a Zenodo DOI, so it is
# already safe somewhere else.

# Derived from ../home/uclcovid/data/updates by build/extract_text.py, which
# stage 0 established is a pure function of its input: two consecutive runs
# produce an identical digest over all 169 outputs. 1.4 MB.
text/

# Derived from text/ by build/digest.py. A reading aid for stage 1, and stage 1
# is finished. 1.7 MB.
digest/

# Derived from ../home/uclcovid/data/covid_raw.csv by build/data_events.py and
# build/camden_events.py, both of which rewrite their JSON from source.
data_events.json
camden_events.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, and deliberately so:
#
#   batches/       the hand-written work of stage 1, 283 rows read out of 1.09
#                  million characters. Irreplaceable.
#   timeline.toml  eight framing paragraphs and twenty declared lag pairings,
#                  hand-written and existing nowhere else.
#   build/         including make_national_batch.py, whose anchors and notes
#                  are the same kind of hand work as the stage 1 batches.
#   sources/       3.2 MB of fetched primary documents. Re-fetchable only for
#                  as long as those URLs resolve, which is precisely the
#                  assumption this whole project exists to distrust. Kept.
#   data/          the Camden comparator, fetched once from an API that has
#                  already changed shape once.
#   timeline.csv   regenerable from batches/ via add_rows.py, but cheap to keep
#                  and it is what the deliverables are built from.
#   TIMELINE.md    generated, but versioning it makes the diffs reviewable,
#   timeline.html  which is worth more than the 456 KB it costs.
#
# Before this is ever pushed to a public remote, sources/ needs a second look:
# those seven documents are third-party and this project does not own them.
